cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cloudfit-core in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "cloudfit-core: Cloud-agnostic machine type scoring engine for computational workloads"
abstract: >
  cloudfit-core is a pure Python library that scores and ranks cloud instance types
  against a workload profile using a configurable weighted scoring function with
  hard floor filters. It supports five bioinformatics resource archetypes (I/O bound,
  CPU bound, memory bound, GPU, and burst-parallel) and dynamic disk sizing for
  sequencing workloads (BCLConvert, BWA-MEM2, Kraken2, AlphaFold, Nextflow).
  Designed to be cloud-provider-agnostic via a plugin architecture compatible
  with Terraform and OpenTofu data sources.
